# Platform symbols src/engine/ cannot link without: the engine->platform edge,
# enumerated instead of described.
#
# EMPTY, AND THAT IS THE POINT. src/engine/ links with no platform object: it is the
# standalone chess library its header comments claim. `./build.sh engine-standalone`
# proves it by compiling every src/engine/*.c alone and linking them with nothing else.
#
# `zone-check` cannot see this direction -- the array it links (ENGINE_SOURCES) contains
# all of platform/, so the edge is inside its boundary and prose is the only other thing
# that could describe it, which is exactly what drifts.
#
# THE RATCHET: a symbol appearing here that is not in this file fails the gate. Now that
# the file is empty, ANY host dependency added to engine/ fails it. The fix is a seam,
# never an edit to this file -- the engine names what it needs and the host registers an
# implementation:
#
#   output_sink.h    search_set_output          the line sink
#   option_source.h  search_set_option_source   the UCI option table
#   time_source.h    search_set_time_source     the monotonic clock
#   arena_source.h   search_set_arena_source    the page allocator for the big arenas
#   worker_set.h     worker_pool_install        the Lazy-SMP worker set
#
# Three things have to hold together or the symbol stays in the link line: the engine
# declares the pointer, EVERY reader in the zone goes through it, and the host registers
# the implementation before the first search.
